-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",77,{
[2433]="70053DBE\n1\tDefeat vengeful wraiths in Emyn Duir (total: 4)\tWraiths can be found in Emyn Duir. You should defeat wraiths, vengeful and otherwise, that plague the land.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated wraiths.\n",
[2434]="70042EB0\n1\tSpeak with Anborn\tAnborn can be found in the keep at Bâr Húrin. You should speak with Anborn.\n2\tDefeat Yambahul\tYambahul can be found somewhere in Southern Ithilien. You should defeat Yambahul.\n3\tSpeak with Anborn\tAnborn can be found in the keep at Bâr Húrin. You should speak with Anborn.\n",
[2435]="70071AD4\n1\tDefeat Újumai the Earth-stirrer\tÚjumai the Earth-stirrer roams the highlands of Padugâsha in An Shêru, north-east of the Spent-lodes.\n2\tTalk to Halshûm in Khanâg Gur\tYou have defeated Újumai the Earth-stirrer. You should return to Khanâg Gur to collect your reward.\n",
[2436]="70034D29\n1\tFree cows in Gárnoth's Farm (0/9)\tThe cows left behind at Gárnoth's Farm are grazing in pens throughout the farm.\n2\tThe Orcs occupying Gárnoth's Farm have managed to keep many cows corralled. They seem to be using them as a local food source instead of relying on shipments from elsewhere.\t\n3\tCompleted\tThe Orcs can no longer rely on the local food source, and will once again have to rely on shipments from elsewhere.\n",
[2437]="70042E97\n1\tMake bundles of arrows (total: 8)\030Repair bows (total: 4)\tWorkbenches can be found in Bâr Húrin. You should repair bows and make bundles of arrows.\n2\tDeliver bundles of arrows (total: 8)\tEmpty quivers can be found in Bâr Húrin. You should fill the quivers with arrows.\n3\tSpeak with Thurindol\tThurindol can be found in the keep at Bâr Húrin. You should talk to Thurindol.\n",
[2438]="7006944E\n1\tComplete Umbar Woodworker's Guild daily orders (total: 5)\tComplete requests from the Umbar Woodworker's Guild. You can acquire these quests from the Umbar Woodworker's Guild Leader in the Umbar Baharbêl craft guild hall.\n2\tCompleted\tYou completed many Umbar woodworker requests.\n",
[2439]="7002EF4B\n1\tCollect bows from Orcs or Uruks in the East Wall (total: 5)\tOrc and Uruk-archers can be found throughout the East Wall. Utlac has asked you to defeat Orcs or Uruks throughout the East Wall and to take their bows so he can destroy them.\n2\tBring Orc-bows to Utlac\tUtlac is at the Rohirrim-camp in the East Wall. You have recovered many crude bows from the Orcs that inhabit the East Wall and should bring them to Utlac so he can destroy them.\n3\tThrow the Orc-bows on the camp-fire near Utlac\tA camp-fire near Utlac is just the place to burn the Orc-bows you have taken. Utlac cannot bear to handle the Orc-bows any longer and has asked you to burn them in a nearby camp-fire.\n4\tTalk to Utlac\tUtlac is at the Rohirrim-encampment, waiting to speak with you.\n",
[2440]="7002C8E1\n1\tSharpen swords (total: 5)\030Sharpen spears (total: 5)\030Reinforce the camp's fortifications (total: 5)\tSwords, spears, and barricades can be found around Wynmar's southern camp. You should help the men of Stangard prepare for the imminent attack.\n2\tReturn to Rothulf\tRothulf is at Wynmar's camp in the south of Thinglad. You should tell Rothulf that you have assisted with preparations for the imminent Orc-attack.\n",
[2441]="7002FDCA\n1\tCollect piles of logs outside Snowbourn (total: 6)\030Collect leather-scraps in Snowbourn (total: 6)\030Collect spears in Snowbourn (total: 3)\tPiles of logs can be found near felled trees outside the walls, while spears and leather can be gathered within the city. Léofhelm has asked you to gather the materials needed to supply Snowbourn.\n2\tBring the supplies to Léofhelm\tLéofhelm can be found in the Mead Hall of Snowbourn. You should return to Léofhelm and let him know that you have done as he asked.\n",
[2442]="70042F5C\n1\tCollect barrels of weapons at the ruined armoury (total: 8)\tThe ruins of the armoury can be found in south-western Osgiliath. Meldir has asked you to recover hidden stores of weapons from the ruins of the armoury.\n2\tDeliver the weapons to Meldir\tMeldir can be found along the south-western walls of Osgiliath. You have recovered many weapons, and should now deliver them to Meldir.\n",
[2443]="70066D03\n1\tCollect boar belly (total: 8)\030Put down diseased boars (total: 6)\tCúronel has asked you to bring her boar belly meat from healthy boars and to put down diseased boars at her farm, Munadhor Farm in Pinnath Gelin.\n2\tReturn to Cúronel\tYou should return to Cúronel with the boar belly pieces that you gathered. Cúronel is at Munadhor Farm, in central Pinnath Gelin.\n",
[2444]="70035590\n1\tTalk to Mossbeard\tMossbeard can be found somewhere past Finglas' Mead far to the south-west of the Stonecliff. Barallas wants you to search for the last Ent that has not rejoined the others at their hideout.\n",
[2445]="7003A656\n1\tFind Dúnburg south of Underharrow\tDúnburg can be found to the south of Underharrow amidst the trees. Ellen Fremedon has asked you to find Dúnburg and send her back to Underharrow.\n2\tTalk to Ellen Fremedon\tEllen Fremedon can be found outside the Mead Hall at Underharrow. You have rescued Dúnburg and sent her on her way. You should return to Ellen Fremedon.\n",
[2446]="700586D3\n1\tComplete 'Implements of Striking' for Hunward\030Complete 'Articles of Durability' for Hunward\tHunward at Trader's Wharf in the Wildwood has agreed to fashion you fine equipment suitable for a legendary Brawler, if you will bring him the materials he needs.\n2\tTalk to Hunward at Trader's Wharf\tHunward is at Trader's Wharf in the Wildwood.\n",
[2447]="70044D78\n1\tDefeat Kamabhosh\030Defeat Uruk-hai lieutenants (total: 3)\tKamabhosh and his lieutenants can be found in the Cisterns. You should find and defeat Kamabhosh and his lieutenants.\n",
[2448]="70044D79\n1\tCollect rubble (total: 9)\tRubble can be found throughout the Cisterns. You should collect rubble for sealing off the mountain entrance to the Cisterns that the Orcs must have used.\n2\tSeal the breach in the Cisterns\tThe mountain entrance to the Cisterns can be found at the northern end of the Cisterns. You should seal off the mountain entrance to the Cisterns that the Orcs used to enter the city.\n",
[2449]="70044D76\n1\tDefeat Orcs (total: 14)\tOrcs can be found throughout the Cisterns. You should defeat Orcs in the Cisterns.\n",
[2450]="70044D73\n1\tThe Withered Tree can be found in the Cisterns. You should try and talk some sense into members of the Withered Tree.\t\n",
[2451]="70044D72\n1\tDestroy papers (total: 8)\tThe Withered Tree can be found in the Cisterns. You should find and destroy documents belonging to the Withered Tree.\n",
[2452]="7003694E\n1\tDefeat the waves of attackers assailing the gate-house ([see journal]/6)\tA gate-house between the Wall and the Hornburg has been converted into a makeshift ward used to treat wounded soldiers. The final doorway leading to the Hornburg has been sealed, but the enemy seeks to breech the opening while slaughtering the wounded in the gatehouse along the way. This rearmost door must be defended at all costs. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2453]="700381C0\n1\tDefeat the waves of attackers assailing the gate-house ([see journal]/6)\tThe enemy plans to breach the Hornburg through a gate-house being used as a makeshift infirmary for the wounded. The wounded men and the supplies of bandages and medicines are in danger, but the door to the Hornburg must be protected at all costs. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[2454]="7001B71A\n1\tClaim the First Ward\tThe First Ward is the first step on the road to taking the Necromancer's Gate.\n2\tClaim the Second Ward\tThe Second Ward provides a vantage point over all of Mirkwood below. It is crucial to take so that reinforcements may approach in safety.\n3\tClaim the Third Ward\tThe courtyard of the Third Ward guards the entrances to several inner chambers of the fortress, most bunks for the Enemy's legions.\n4\tClaim the Fourth Ward\tThe Fourth Ward is a seemingly ramshackle arrangement of tents and debris, but a number of the Enemy's leaders camp there to stay close to their troops.\n5\tClaim the Sorcerer's Ascent\tThe Sorcerer's Ascent is the final defence of the Necromancer's Gate and is well fortified on a steep incline.\n6\tClaim the Necromancer's Gate\tThe Necromancer's Gate guards the heart of Dol Guldur's defences. It must fall in order to besiege the true fortress.\n",
[2455]="70029FC0\n1\tComplete 'Breaching the Necromancer's Gate' in a raid group\tThe Necromancer's Gate marks the entrance to the heart of Dol Guldur's outer fortifications. To assault the fortress, the gate must fall.\n",
[2456]="70062E83\n1\tCollect Orc-bows from Caranost scouts (total: 5)\tMaedhril asked you to defeat Caranost scouts and retrieve their bows.\n2\tBurn the Orc-bows in the bonfire atop the tower overlooking the bridge at Caranost\tThe tower overlooking the bridge at Caranost holds a large bonfire at which Maedhril wanted you to burn the Orc-bows.\n3\tTalk to Maedhril at Sírlond\tMaedhril is at Sírlond, east of Caranost proper.\n",
[2457]="7002827D\n1\tDestroy banners (total: 3)\tYou should seek out and destroy any banners that you find in the area.\n",
[2458]="7002827B\n1\tDefeat sentries (total: 5)\tLhan Gogledh lies along the path north of Lhucu's hut. Lhucu has asked you to seek out and defeat the sentries that patrol the outskirts of Lhan Gogledh.\n2\tTalk to Lhucu at her hut\tLhucu is at her hut, south of Lhan Gogledh. You should inform Lhucu that the sentries have been scattered.\n",
[2459]="700096FA\n1\tBring the supplies to Alfred Whitley\tAlfred Whitley can be found in Men Erain, south of Tinnudir across the lake. Following the shore road north and east into Men Erain, Whitley's camp can be found on the hillside up some carved stone steps. The Ranger Helechír has asked you to bring supplies to a man by the name of Alfred Whitley in Men Erain.\n2\tCollect journal from Alfred Whitley's camp\tAlfred Whitley is missing from his watch-post in Men Erain, but the journal that remains among his things may hold some clue to his whereabouts. You found Alfred Whitley's watch-post, but there was no sign of Whitley himself. His journal may hold some clue as to his fate.\n3\tBring the supplies and journal back to Helechír\tHelechír is on an island a little south-west of Men Erain. You found the journal of a Ranger on a pilgrimage to his family's ancestral holdings near Annúminas. According to his journal, he suspected he was being followed. Helechír will be most interested to hear of this.\n",
[2460]="70000756\n1\tLocate the cave\tThe meeting cave is in the Orc-encampment of Cirith Nûr, north-west of the Old Greenway Fort. Andreg has tasked you with finding the cave where the brigands and Orcs plan to meet and defeat their leaders.\n2\tEnter the cave\tYou have found the cave. Now all that remains is to enter it, disperse the brigands and Orcs, and defeat their leaders.\n3\tTalk to Andreg at the Old Greenway Fort\tAndreg is at the Old Greenway Fort, south-east of Cirith Nûr. You should bring news of your success to Andreg at once.\n",
[2461]="70033126\n1\tDefeat Yûl\tYûl can be found on the highest floor of Hurmulkezer in the south-eastern Flaming Deeps, south of Durin's Court. You should find and defeat Yûl.\n2\tDefeat Yûl\tYûl can be found on the highest floor of Hurmulkezer in the south-eastern Flaming Deeps, south of Durin's Court. You should find and defeat Yûl.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Yûl, the leader of the Ghâsh-hai forces in Hurmulkezer. While many Orcs still remain, they will founder without a leader.\n",
[2462]="7004CE3F\n1\tDefeat Lake-town knife-throwers (total: 5)\030Defeat Lake-town Smugglers (total: 10)\tLake-town Smugglers and knife-throwers can be found inside the Smugglers' hideout in Lake-town. You should defeat Lake-town Smugglers and knife-throwers.\n2\tTalk to Dagrun\tDagrun can be found in the Council of Wares Headquarters. You should talk to Dagrun.\n",
[2463]="7003A5DE\n1\tTravel to the Boar-tribe Orc-lair\tThe entrance to the Boar-tribe lair is south of Beaconwatch, not far from the Mering-Stream. Cúthing wants you to travel to the Boar-tribe lair and defeat the chieftain.\n2\tDefeat Pakon, the Maldorr Orc-chieftain\tThe Boar-tribe chieftain is somewhere within their lair. If you encounter the chieftain of the Boar-tribe, defeat him.\n3\tTalk to Cúthing\tCúthing is standing near Meregyth, outside the Mead Hall of Beaconwatch. You should return to Beaconwatch and tell Cúthing about your victory.\n",
[2464]="70049561\n1\tDefeat foes at Orodir (total: 10)\030Destroy shackles (total: 10)\tOrodir is located next to Naerband. You should destroy shackles and defeat foes in Orodir.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated foes and destroyed shackles.\n",
})
